{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver's admissible position evidence places him outside the POL-NS-02 arrival radius but far inside the POL-NS-03 ceiling: derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count is 0 against 68 driver fixes, while his closest recorded approach to the pickup pin is 102.77 m — not more than 400 m from the pin, and within the LARGE_VENUE 120 m radius on raw distance. This is a driver who came to the venue and stood at the wrong face of it, which is the case POL-NS-03 exists to decide; POL-NS-02 only makes the opening distance test.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00404", "EV-TRIP-00404"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver held his pickup attempt at Bayshore Park past the free waiting period in force. The trace carries a stationary speed reading (0.0 kph in derived.driver_track.distinct_speeds_kph), and the trip record's own wait measure is 5.5 minutes (wait_time_min 5.5, arrived_at 18:51:25 to cancelled_at 18:56:55) against the 300 second free_wait_sec the platform policy in force sets for this LARGE_VENUE trip, so the required dwell was served before the driver cancelled.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00404", "EV-TRIP-00404"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.distinct_speeds_kph",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The mislocation is pin ambiguity, not driver fault. The pickup carries venue_id VEN-BAYSHORE-PARK and the trip record states registered_pickup_points of 2, while the pin label identifies only one of them ('Guardhouse A, 60 Bayshore Rd'). Under POL-NS-03(ii) neither party specified the sub-location, so the mislocation is attributed to the pin, and the driver is entitled to the platform-funded goodwill payment of 50 percent of the cancellation fee — S$2.00, which is the figure the fare record's own money block carries.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00404", "EV-FARE-00404"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.goodwill",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-03(i) cannot strip that goodwill. It applies only where the rider stated the correct entrance, block or tower in the chat_log, and the rider's only message in the waiting window is 'coming' at 18:52:15, which names no guardhouse, gate, block, tower or bay. Limb (i) is therefore not engaged, and limb (ii) allocates the mislocation to the ambiguous pin.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00404", "EV-TRIP-00404"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider on this record. Limb (a) requires a rider message whose content locates or coordinates — the rider's own position, an entrance, block, tower or bay identifier, a request for the driver's position, or a statement that the rider cannot see the vehicle. The single word 'coming' (MSG-00404-003, 18:52:15) states none of those, so limb (a) fails and the clause cannot be used to deny the driver the POL-NS-03(ii) goodwill.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00404", "EV-TRIP-00404"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-NS-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No false-arrival finding is made out against the driver under POL-NS-05. That clause catches a marker struck more than 300 m from the pin or while travelling at 15 kph or more; the exported record pairs no distance or speed reading with the 18:51:25 arrival event, the driver's closest recorded approach is 102.77 m from the pin — well inside the 300 m line — and the platform's own arrival notice followed at 18:51:26. A marker corroborated by an arrival notice and a 5.5 minute wait is not a fabricated arrival.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00404", "EV-TRIP-00404", "EV-CHAT-00404"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver does not contest the fee. POL-NS-01 limb (d) is not satisfied on the reason code recorded: DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE is the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider, and the clause expressly excludes it, so the cancellation fee cannot stand under POL-NS-01 and the full refund of the S$4.00 follows from POL-NS-03's first sentence. That reason code was in any event the truthful one for a wrong-guardhouse cancellation, unlike a no-show code the driver did not claim.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00404", "EV-FARE-00404"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The outcome the driver seeks is the compound one POL-GEN-03 provides for: the contested S$4.00 cancellation fee refunded in full to the rider, with S$2.00 driver compensation paid by the platform under POL-NS-03(ii) and never recovered from the rider, the two amounts independent and not netted. POL-GEN-03 names POL-NS-03(ii) pin-ambiguity goodwill as the standard instance of this split.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00404", "EV-TRIP-00404"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The case is decidable now and needs no human hold. POL-NS-07's anti-farming check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d is 1 against completed_trips_30d of 120 — 1 is below the 4 threshold and 1/120 = 0.008 is below the 0.08 rate — and no POL-NS-09 trigger is present, since disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both profiles and the rider's no_show_disputes_30d is 0, so neither limb (c) nor limb (d) is engaged and the money can issue on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00404", "EV-RPROF-00404"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 2.0,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "Rider: your S$4.00 cancellation fee is refunded in full. Driver: an independent, platform-funded goodwill payment of S$2.00 is made to you; it is never recovered from the rider and is not netted against the refund.\n\nThe charge cannot stand. The trip was terminated by the driver under cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE (EV-TRIP-00404). POL-NS-01(d) recognises only RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT, and says in terms that DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE is the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider. The waiting limb fails too: POL-NS-01(c) measures the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, and EV-GPS-00404 contains none (qualifying_fix_count 0 of 68 fixes; longest qualifying run 0.0 s) against the 300 s free_wait_sec the record's platform_policy carries, so POL-NS-06 shows a 300-second shortfall and the fee is refunded. The sum refunded is the S$4.00 the ledger actually charged (EV-FARE-00404: cancellation_fee 4.00, total_charged 4.00, refund_issued 0.00; no booking or platform fee).\n\nThe driver is still paid, under POL-NS-03. His closest recorded approach is 102.77 m from the pin and the trace shows no held position inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius — the wrong face of the same venue, within the 400 m ceiling, and the distance test that carries the clause is satisfied. Bayshore Park records registered_pickup_points 2 (EV-TRIP-00404) and the pin names only 'Guardhouse A'; the chat log (EV-CHAT-00404) holds one rider message, 'coming' at 18:52:15, naming no guardhouse, gate, block, tower or bay, and the driver's own statement that the pin showed the condo but not which gate is evidence to the same effect. His stationary wait at that gate runs from the 18:51:25 arrival event to the 18:56:55 cancellation (5.5 minutes, EV-TRIP-00404), which meets the 300 s required dwell. POL-NS-03(i) is therefore not engaged; limb (ii) applies, the mislocation is attributed to the ambiguous pin, and the goodwill is 50 percent (pin_ambiguity_goodwill_rate 0.5) of S$4.00 = S$2.00, the figure the money block carries.\n\nThe rider's remaining claims do not change this. POL-NS-04 is rejected: limb (a) requires a message whose content locates or coordinates (the rider's own position, an entrance, block, tower or bay, a request for the driver's position, or a statement that she cannot see the vehicle), and 'coming' states none of them, so her 37 clean rider fixes never come into play. POL-NS-06's bar on 'driver compensation' concerns the POL-NS-07 payout on a refunded fee; it does not reach the separate, platform-funded POL-NS-03(ii) goodwill. POL-NS-12 does not apply because the arrival marker is BUTTON, not GPS_AUTO, so wait_time_min 5.5 cannot stand in for GPS dwell.\n\nNo false-arrival referral is made: no distance or speed is paired with the 18:51:25 marker and the closest recorded approach (102.77 m) is far inside POL-NS-05's 300 m line. Nothing is impaired — trip record, GPS trace, chat log and fare ledger are all weight 1.0 and the fare line reconciles with the fee in force; the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00404-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT), disclosed by the rider, and its absence only makes POL-NS-06(i) accumulation unavailable. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires (no direct contradiction between admissible artifacts, no counterparty disputes on either profile, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check is not met: 1 termination against 120 completed trips, rate 0.008), so confidence (0.85) is above the 0.70 floor. The total monetary effect is S$6.00, below the S$8.00 execution threshold, so this provisional ruling executes automatically; either party may appeal once within 30 days."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

