    "confidence": 0.8,
    "explanation": "Decision for both parties. Your accounts agree and the record backs them: the pin at Bayshore Park identified the condominium but not which of its two guardhouses, the driver waited at the other gate, and the rider was at Guardhouse A where the pin sits.\n\n1) The $4.00 fee is refunded in full to the rider. POL-NS-01 needs all four of its conditions and three of them fail. No qualifying position fix falls inside the 120 m arrival radius for this LARGE_VENUE pickup - 0 of the driver's 68 fixes (EV-GPS-00404) - so limb (b) fails. The qualifying in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds against the 300-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec on EV-TRIP-00404, and the derived minimum_dwell_sec for LARGE_VENUE), a 300-second shortfall (EV-GPS-00404), so limb (c) fails; POL-NS-06 would refund on that shortfall alone, and POL-NS-02 reaches the same refund because no qualifying in-radius fix exists. The trip was also terminated under cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, which limb (d) expressly does not recognise. The amount refunded is the cancellation-fee line actually charged and nothing else: $4.00 (EV-FARE-00404, cancellation_fee 4.00, total_charged 4.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00).\n\n2) The driver's payment is fixed by POL-NS-03, not by POL-NS-01 or POL-NS-07. The trace shows the driver holding position for the required waiting period outside the 120 m arrival radius (his fixes include a stationary 0.0 kph reading, the record's wait is 5.5 minutes = 330 seconds against the 300-second minimum, and the derived block records 0 intervals in which he held position inside the radius), and his closest recorded approach, 102.77 m, sits well within POL-NS-03's 400 m ceiling; this is the wrong-face-of-the-same-venue case POL-NS-03 exists to decide, and POL-NS-02 yields to it on compensation. Fault is allocated from the chat log: the rider's only message was 'coming' at 18:52:15 (MSG-00404-003) and it names no guardhouse, gate, block, tower or bay, so POL-NS-03(i) does not strip compensation; registered_pickup_points is 2 while neither party named a sub-location, so under POL-NS-03(ii) the mislocation is attributed to pin ambiguity, and the driver receives the platform-funded goodwill of 50 percent of the $4.00 fee - $2.00. That sum is charged to the platform and never recovered from the rider; the refund and the goodwill are independent and are not netted (POL-GEN-03).\n\n3) The rider's POL-NS-04 argument is not accepted. Limb (a) requires a rider message whose content locates or coordinates - the rider's own position, an entrance, block, tower or bay identifier, a request for the driver's position, or a statement that she cannot see the vehicle. 'coming' is none of these and gives the driver nothing to act on, so the clause does not exonerate the rider and does not remove the goodwill. The rider's later statement that she was at Guardhouse A was made in her dispute filing, after the trip, not in the chat log, so it does not engage POL-NS-03(i) either.\n\n4) No referral is entered. POL-NS-05 does not fire: the record pairs no distance or speed reading with the 18:51:25 arrival event, and the closest recorded approach (102.77 m) is inside the 300 m line, so no false-arrival finding is made and POL-NS-05(ii) is not triggered. POL-NS-01's driver-education referral does not fire either, because the driver's stationary fixes do not lie inside the arrival radius. The arrival marker was a driver button press, not GPS_AUTO, so POL-NS-12 cannot make the platform's arrival or wait-timer events a substitute for the geofence dwell POL-NS-01(b) and (c) require.\n\n5) Nothing is escalated. The GPS trace, trip record, chat log and fare ledger are all COMPLETE at weight 1.0; the trace has 100 percent coverage with no gaps at a 10-second cadence; the chat holds exactly the 4 messages the trip record records; the fare line reconciles with the $4.00 fee in platform_policy; and no POL-NS-09 trigger fires - no disputes between these parties in 90 days, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (1 termination against 120 completed trips, a rate of 0.008). The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00404-01, weight 0.0) can carry no fact and only makes POL-NS-06(i) accumulation unavailable, which changes nothing here. Every deciding fact rests on weight-1.0 artifacts, so confidence is 0.80. The monetary effect is $4.00 refunded plus $2.00 goodwill - $6.00 in all, below the $8.00 execution threshold - so it executes automatically."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 2.0,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: you were both at Bayshore Park on 19 Aug, at two different guardhouses. The SGD 4.00 cancellation fee cannot stand, and because this is a wrong-entrance case rather than a rider no-show, the driver is also paid a platform-funded goodwill sum. The two amounts are independent and are not netted against each other (POL-GEN-03); the ruling value names the outcome for the filing party, the rider.\n\nWHY THE FEE IS REFUNDED. The driver terminated the trip at 18:56:55 under reason code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE (EV-TRIP-00404). POL-NS-01(d) recognises only RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE and EXCESSIVE_WAIT, and states that DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE is the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider: limb (d) fails on the driver's own record, so the fee is not chargeable. The GPS evidence agrees on the arrival side: of 68 driver fixes, 0 qualify within the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius and the longest in-geofence run is 0.0 s (EV-GPS-00404), so POL-NS-02 deems no arrival and POL-NS-01(b) fails; and the in-geofence dwell is 0 s against the 300 s free waiting period in force (EV-TRIP-00404 platform_policy.free_wait_sec 300; minimum_dwell_sec 300 for LARGE_VENUE), a 300 s shortfall under POL-NS-06. The refund is the cancellation-fee line only, SGD 4.00, the sum the ledger charged and still holds (EV-FARE-00404: cancellation_fee 4.00, total_charged 4.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). The driver's 5.5 minute wait (wait_time_min 5.5) is not in-geofence GPS dwell and cannot supply limb (c), and because the arrival marker is the driver's own button press, not GPS_AUTO, POL-NS-12 does not apply and no platform wait-timer event stands in for the GPS clock.\n\nWHY THE DRIVER IS PAID SGD 2.00. POL-NS-01 then asks where the driver's stationary position lay. The trace shows no in-geofence hold, and his closest recorded approach was 102.77 m from the pin (EV-GPS-00404, derived.driver_track.min_distance_m) - outside the arrival radius on the admissible fixes but inside POL-NS-03's 400 m ceiling. The trip carries registered_pickup_points 2 with the pin labelled 'Bayshore Park, Guardhouse A, 60 Bayshore Rd' (EV-TRIP-00404); the driver held his position for the required period (wait_time_min 5.5, 330 s, 18:51:25 to 18:56:55); he concedes 'Bayshore has two guardhouses. Pin showed the condo, not which gate'; and the chat log (EV-CHAT-00404) shows neither party naming a guardhouse, gate, block or bay. POL-NS-03 therefore governs: the SGD 4.00 is refunded in full to the rider, and under limb (ii) the mislocation is attributed to pin ambiguity, so the driver receives a platform-funded goodwill payment of 50 percent of the fee - SGD 2.00 (EV-FARE-00404 money block, goodwill 2.00) - charged to the platform and never recovered from the rider. Limb (i) does not take it away: the rider's only message, 'coming' at 18:52:15, names no entrance, block, tower or bay.\n\nCLAIMS I DID NOT ACCEPT. The rider's POL-NS-04 claim fails at limb (a): that clause requires a message whose content locates or coordinates - the rider's own position, an entrance/block/tower/bay, a request for the driver's position, or a statement that the vehicle cannot be seen - and 'coming' is none of those, so POL-NS-04 neither exonerates the rider nor removes the goodwill. The rider's POL-NS-05 claim also fails: no distance or speed is paired with the 18:51:25 arrival event in the record, the driver's recorded position is within 300 m of the pin and his hold served the required period, and the platform's own arrival notice followed at 18:51:26, so the marker is not shown false and no false-arrival referral is made under POL-NS-05(ii). No clause here produces any other referral.\n\nWHAT I CHECKED ON THE EVIDENCE. No artifact is impaired at policy level under POL-NS-08: the trace is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 with 100 percent coverage, 10 s cadence, no gaps, 68 driver and 37 rider fixes; the chat log holds exactly the 4 messages the trip record counts; and the ledger's 4.00 reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd 4.00. The only artifact below 1.0 is the MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00404-01, weight 0.0, whose absence is itself citable: it makes POL-NS-06(i) accumulation unavailable and exonerates nobody, and it carries no deciding fact. Every fact this ruling rests on sits on weight-1.0 artifacts, so confidence is 0.85 against a cap of 1.00 and above the 0.70 floor. No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger fires: nothing contradicts on arrival, dwell or rider presence; both profiles show 0 disputes between the two of you and the rider 0 no-show disputes in the trailing 30 days; and POL-NS-07's anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 1 against completed_trips_30d 120, rate 0.008). The monetary effect is SGD 6.00 (SGD 4.00 refunded to the rider plus SGD 2.00 platform goodwill to the driver), below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes on issue; either of you may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
